# Patches must reach the Windows runner byte-for-byte: git apply fails on CRLF-converted
# context lines. Upstream hit the same class of bug (see their "ci: disable autocrlf" and
# "ci: use .gitattributes instead" commits on _meta_win_clang_portable.yaml).
*.patch -text
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Same class of bug, one step removed: verify-binary.sh reads patches/jellyfin-ffmpeg/checks/*.checks
# field by field, and a CRLF checkout leaves the CR on the LAST field of every line -- turning
# `dolbyvision` into a pattern that can never match. That would fail only the two windows jobs, and
# only after a 2.5 hour build. The parser also strips CR; this is the other lock on the same door.
*.checks text eol=lf
